  <section>
    <h2>Behaviour in Amstelvar Avar2</h2>
    <p>
      Amstelvar Avar2 implements XTEQ through separate horizontal round counter-shaping
      axes for uppercase, lowercase, and figures. The transformation changes
      the horizontal balance of a round counter by adjusting the horizontal
      curve handles, without intentionally changing the rest of the glyph.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Uppercase round construction — O</h2>
    <p>
      O is the primary control glyph. XTEQ makes its internal counter more
      elliptical or more squared in the horizontal direction while the outside
      form and overall width remain stable.
    </p>

